:"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/The_Sun_at_perihelion_and_aphelion.jpg/500px-The_Sun_at_perihelion_and_aphelion.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Angular size of the Sun at Earth's orbital periapsis called perihelion (max./closest, 2. to 5. January) and at apoapsis called aphelion (min./furthest, 3. to 6. July). The resulting 7% difference in solar intensity does not overpower geographic factors of climate, with seasons staying more moderate on the Southern Hemisphere due to having less landmass.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Sun_at_perihelion_and_aphelion.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Hemisphere_land.png/500px-Hemisphere_land.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Hemisphere_land.png/1280px-Hemisphere_land.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Hemisphere_land.png/500px-Hemisphere_land.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHemisphere_land.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Hemisphere_water.png/500px-Hemisphere_water.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Hemisphere_water.png/1280px-Hemisphere_water.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Hemisphere_water.png/500px-Hemisphere_water.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHemisphere_water.png"}],"sounds":{}}}